    <!-- 19 PRESENT CONTINUOUS -->
    <section class="screen">
      <span class="tag lo">Right now · present continuous</span>
      <h2>estar + the gerund</h2>
      <p>When you want to stress that something is happening <b>at this very moment</b>, use <span class="es">estar</span> + the <b>gerund</b> (the "-ing" form):</p>
      <div class="eqn"><span class="es">estar</span> + gerund<small>-ar → -ando &nbsp;·&nbsp; -er / -ir → -iendo</small></div>
      <ul>
        <li><span class="es">trabajar</span> → <span class="hl e">estoy trabajando</span> — I <b>am working</b> (right now).</li>
        <li><span class="es">comer</span> → <span class="hl e">está comiendo</span> — he <b>is eating</b>.</li>
        <li><span class="es">escribir</span> → <span class="hl e">estamos escribiendo</span> — we <b>are writing</b>.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="note"><b>Don't overuse it.</b> For habits and general truths, plain present is better: <span class="es">Estudio español</span> ("I study / am studying Spanish" in general), <b>not</b> <span class="es">estoy estudiando</span> unless you mean at this exact second. A few gerunds are irregular: <span class="es">leer → leyendo</span>, <span class="es">dormir → durmiendo</span>, <span class="es">pedir → pidiendo</span>.</p>
    </section>

